  "description": "NY drill: Brooklyn's drill at 138 to 146 BPM felt at half time: heavy 808s that slide and bounce between octaves under a sparse kick, the drill snare on beat three answered late, skippy hats in threes with rolls, a dark choir or strings, a minor piano figure or a flipped R&B sample, a bell or flute line in the hooks",
